            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Latin for a kiss on the lips, then the Latin for an embrace."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: amplector, amplectī",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "amplector, amplectī — \"to embrace, hug\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Pater fīlium redeuntem amplectitur. The father embraces his son as he comes home."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Deponent: amplector, amplectī, amplexus sum: ambi- 'around' + plectō 'to twine'. Also to welcome an idea."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "amplector is built on ambi- \"around\" and plector, from plectō \"to twine, plait\" (EtymDB): to wind the arms around."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
