              "text": "complector, complectī — \"to clasp, embrace; to include\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Amīcī post longum tempus sē complectuntur. The friends embrace after a long time."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Deponent: complector, complectī, complexus sum. Also to take in, to include. English complex comes from its participle."
            }
          ]
        },
